  "rating": {
    "inherent": "moderate",
    "residual": "low",
    "forecast": "moderate",
    "rationale": "The present design exposes only a trusted employee input to a read-only internal policy index and a reply channel structurally bound to the authenticated requester. Structural independent controls sever broader exfiltration paths: replies cannot be redirected, the client has no hidden fetch behavior, and network egress is denied and pen-test verified. Forecast risk rises to moderate if reply routing is loosened or a new outbound channel is added, because the current low residual depends primarily on the destination-binding control."
  },
